CC : CCE , CCB , BBS/O , COO , WSE , WSI , WOG , WSG , Others Listed

good day sir ,

Draft situation / vessel arrival -berthing position as on date.
========================================
> The draft cut situation for CCU has slightly improved until the next few days 19/11 (6.4M) ; 20/11 (6.4M) ; 21/11 ( 6.3M) ; 22/11 (6.2M) for outward sailings.

> Over n above the given draft position,  Day to Day draft position will be announced by Marine Department till draft situation is normal.

> Situation is likely to improve over the next few days as dredging activities have commenced in navigational channel and other areas in river Hooghly .

> Kolkata Port however announced that situation is well within control and this draft cut is a common factor for any riverine port and it has only

   aggravated due to prolonged monsoon / excessive flooding at few districts, resulting in sludge & mud formation in the navigational channels.

> To keep close tab of the situation, Ministry of Surface Transport has advised Marine Dept, to form a core team to review on the dredging and keep

   informed about the day to day progress.

> No draft cut at Haldia till 23-Nov-2013.

> 4 ships ( incl. 2 chs vsl ) sailed this morning at 6.4M draft.

> Currently 4 vessels ( incl 1 CHS vsls)  are working at berth. Further 4 vessels ( incl 2 CHS vsls)  scheduled to arrive for berthing on 19/11.

> Currently, laden & mty space is allotted by CHS partners as per BSA quota to HJS. However, additional space / tonnage is difficult to obtain until draft normalcy.

> O/B allocation is being done on restricted basis ( Due to limited space , CCUBS offc is following BBG instruction , and emphasis is being given on Yield Management )

> On Winter Surcharge , no official announcements still made by any Shipping Lines ( few major carriers viz Maersk/MSC/APL/NYK/EMC/YML/Happag will not apply

   for this temporary draft cut ) .

> As per WSI Guideline Hjs has announced Winter Surcharge for INHDA , for INCCU O/B is being accepted subject to CMPB Guideline of Usd 350/teu .

> Effective 1/11/2013 , full R/R ( Usd 200/300/300 per D2/D4/D5 )  has been announced for NE/ME basis WSE guideline .

> Situation likely to be normal in Wk 49 .

> To avoid surplus inventory situation Mty Repo to commence from Wk 47  subject to approval .





Regards
Gaurav Sengupta
CCUBSG .

