<div><font face="">Draft situation / vessel arrival -berthing position as on date.</font></div>
<div><font face="">========================================</font> </div>
<font face="">
<div><font face="">&gt; The draft cut situation for CCU has slightly improved&nbsp;until the next few days 19/11 (6.4M) ; 20/11 (6.4M) ; 21/11 ( 6.3M) ; 22/11 (6.2M) for outward sailings.</font></div>
</font>
<p><font face="">&gt; Over n above the given draft position, &nbsp;<font face="">Day to Day draft position will be announced by Marine Department till draft situation is normal.</font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face="">&gt;&nbsp;S<font face="">ituation is likely to improve over the next few days as dredging activities have commenced&nbsp;in&nbsp;navigational channel&nbsp;and other areas in&nbsp;river Hooghly .</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; Kolkata Port however&nbsp;announced that situation is well within control and this draft cut is a common factor for any riverine port&nbsp;and it&nbsp;has&nbsp;</font></font></font><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">only</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp; </font>&nbsp;aggravated&nbsp;due&nbsp;to prolonged monsoon / excessive flooding&nbsp;at few districts, resulting in sludge &amp; mud formation in the navigational channels.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; To keep close tab of the situation, Ministry of Surface Transport has advised Marine Dept, to form a core team&nbsp;to review on the dredging and&nbsp;keep</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp;&nbsp; </font>informed about the day to day progress.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; No draft cut at Haldia till 23-Nov-2013.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt; 4 ships ( incl. 2 chs vsl ) sailed&nbsp;this morning at 6.4M draft.&nbsp;&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt;</font><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp;Currently&nbsp;<font face="">4 vessels ( incl 1 CHS vsls) &nbsp;are working at berth. Further 4 vessels ( incl 2 CHS vsls) &nbsp;scheduled to arrive for berthing on 19/11.</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; Currently, laden &amp; mty space is allotted by CHS partners as per BSA quota to HJS. However, additional space / tonnage is difficult to obtain until draft normalcy.</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; O/B allocation is being done on restricted basis ( Due to limited&nbsp;space , CCUBS offc&nbsp;is following&nbsp;BBG instruction&nbsp;, and emphasis is being given on Yield Management )
</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; On Winter Surcharge , no official announcements still made by any Shipping Lines ( few major carriers viz Maersk/MSC/APL/NYK/EMC/YML/Happag will not apply</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp; </font>
&nbsp;for this temporary draft cut ) .</font></font></font></font></p>
<font face=""><font face=""><font face="">
<p><font face="">&gt; As per WSI Guideline Hjs has announced Winter Surcharge for INHDA&nbsp;, for INCCU&nbsp;O/B is being accepted subject to CMPB Guideline of Usd 350/teu .<font face="">&nbsp;</font>
</p>
<div>
<p>&gt; <font face=""><font face="">Effective 1/11/2013 , full R/R ( Usd 200/300/300 per D2/D4/D5&nbsp;) &nbsp;has been announced for NE/ME basis WSE guideline .</font></font>
</p>
<p><font face="">&gt; </font><font face="">Situation likely to be normal in Wk 49 .</font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt; To avoid surplus inventory situation&nbsp;Mty Repo to commence from Wk 47&nbsp; subject to approval&nbsp;.&nbsp;</font></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
