<font face="">
<div><font face="">&gt; The draft cut situation for CCU remains unchanged until the next few days 17/11 (6.1M) ; 18/11 (6.2M) ; 19/11 ( 6.1M) ; 20/11 (6.2M) for outward sailings.</font></div>
</font>
<p><font face="">&gt; <font face="">Draft cut announced for CCU by 0.3 mtrs to 0.5 mtrs. on day-to-day basis till 21-Nov-2013.</font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face="">&gt;&nbsp;S<font face="">ituation is&nbsp;improving over the next few days as dredging activities have commenced at Rangaphala channel and other areas in the Hooghly channel,</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp;&nbsp; which could further&nbsp;improve the draft conditions, normalcy likely to resume by wk 49 .</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; Kolkata Port however&nbsp;announced that situation is well within control and this draft cut is a common factor for any riverine port&nbsp;and it&nbsp;has&nbsp;</font></font></font><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">only</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp; </font>&nbsp;aggravated&nbsp;due&nbsp;to prolonged monsoon / excessive flooding&nbsp;resulting in sludge &amp; mud formation in the navigational channels.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; To keep close tab of the situation, Ministry of Surface Transport has advised Marine Dept, to form a core team&nbsp;to review on the dredging and&nbsp;keep</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp;&nbsp; </font>informed about the day to day progress.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; No draft cut at Haldia till 23-Nov-2013.</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt; 2 CHS vessels ( KLAR0036E / VEAA0031E ) sailed on 17/11 at 6.1M draft.</font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt;</font><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp;<font face="">Presently 4 vessels ( incl 2 CHS vsls) &nbsp;are working at berth. Further 2 vessels ( incl 1 CHS vsls) &nbsp;scheduled to arrive for berthing on 18/11.</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; Currently, space is allotted by CHS partners as per BSA quota to HJS. However, additional space / tonnage is difficult to obtain until draft normalcy.</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; O/B allocation is being done on restricted basis , due to shortage of space on CHS feeder Vessels .</font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&gt; On Winter Surcharge , no official announcements made by any Shipping Lines ( few major carriers viz Maersk/MSC/APL/NYK/EMC/YML/Happag will not apply</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face=""><font face="">&nbsp; </font>
&nbsp;for this temporary draft cut ) .</font></font></font></font></p>
<p><font face="">&gt; <font face=""><font face="">As per WSI Guideline Hjs has announced Winter Surcharge for INHDA&nbsp;, for INCCU&nbsp;O/B is being accepted subject to CMPB Guideline of Usd 350/teu .</font></font><font face="">&nbsp;</font>
</p>
</div>
<div>
